WEBVTT

00:00.600 --> 00:03.750
This gateway protects sensitive data before cloud reasoning begins.

00:03.800 --> 00:06.950
We enter identity, payment, and private project details.

00:07.000 --> 00:10.150
Shape detection and explicit terms protect every sensitive value.

00:10.200 --> 00:13.250
High-risk values remain withheld unless disclosure is explicit.

00:13.300 --> 00:16.700
The fail-closed gateway pseudonymizes the request before Gemini sees it.

00:16.800 --> 00:19.400
Four independent dimensions explain the release decision.

00:19.500 --> 00:21.800
This is pseudonymization, not anonymization.

00:23.100 --> 00:25.600
The masked pane shows exactly what Gemini received.

00:27.800 --> 00:30.600
A click traces one protected value across the workflow.

00:31.200 --> 00:34.350
Safe values return once, while card data remains withheld.

00:35.800 --> 00:39.300
The OKF record preserves provenance and deterministic leak-check evidence.

00:40.800 --> 00:44.650
The result is useful, inspectable, and never released through an unsafe fallback.

00:46.960 --> 00:48.810
This is Codex in a real pseudo-terminal.

00:50.360 --> 00:52.810
We submit an email address through the Privacy Gateway.

00:53.760 --> 00:56.060
Gemini receives only pseudonymized text.

00:56.360 --> 00:59.160
Deterministic checks pass, and the safe value returns.
